      players: '4 players in two partnerships (sitting opposite).',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck. Ace is high.',
      equipment: 'Standard deck, 14-point pegboard.',
      dealing: 'Deal and play are STRICTLY anti-clockwise. Each player receives 6 cards (usually dealt 3 at a time). The 25th card is turned up for trumps.',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Trump Bonus**: If the turned-up card is an Ace (1 pt), Six (2 pts), or Jack (3 pts), the dealer's team scores immediately. 2. **The Beg**: The player to the dealer's right (Eldest) chooses to 'Stand' or 'Beg'. 3. **The Gift/Run**: If they beg, dealer can gift 1 point to opponents or 'Run the cards' (deal 3 more and flip new trump). Score again for new A/6/J. 4. **Trick Play**: Follow suit or trump. 5. **Counting Out**: Points are scored in order: High, Low, Jack, Game.",
